// Limited (many-to-many) relationship 'Headcount Plan'[Region] *-* Entity[Region].
// A regular relationship adds a blank row on the one side for keys it can't match; a limited one does not:
// "Asia Operations" (planned, no entity yet) gets no row under Region, but the grand total still counts it.
// Expected (DuckDB, FY2013 plan, SYNTHETIC, NOT run in Power BI):
//   European Operations 30, North America Operations 156, Pacific Operations (blank), Eliminations (blank);
//   no blank Region row; total 191 = 186 + 5 for Asia Operations.
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS (
    ROLLUPADDISSUBTOTAL ( Entity[Region], "Is Total" ),
    TREATAS ( { 2013 }, 'Headcount Plan'[Fiscal Year] ),
    "Planned Heads", SUM ( 'Headcount Plan'[Planned Heads] )
)
